  "text": "The longest river in the world is the Nile River.\n\nTo simplify the equation $x/2 - 1/3 = 3x/4 + 5$, we can eliminate the fractions by multiplying every term by the least common multiple (LCM) of the denominators 2, 3, and 4, which is 12.\n\n1. Multiply both sides by 12:\n   $12 \\cdot (x/2) - 12 \\cdot (1/3) = 12 \\cdot (3x/4) + 12 \\cdot 5$\n\n2. Simplify each term:\n   $6x - 4 = 9x + 60$\n\nThe simplified equation is $6x - 4 = 9x + 60$."
